line 6, 11, 16 type: bug SUB-1196 (narrowing a type parameter) narrowing a `T` keeps `T`, where tsc gives `NonNullable<T>` or `T & object`
line 7, 8, 10, 12, 14, 15, 19 type: by-design spec §1.6 `a && b` is `falsy_part(a) | b` and `a || b` is `truthy_part(a) | b`, even when `a`'s truthiness is known
